# Server-managed copy

When deciding where user-facing text belongs, use this test:

- **Would this text need to change when the service behavior changes, without an app release?**
  - If yes: serve it from the API (`GET /managed-copy/:slug`).
  - If no: keep it in the i18n catalog.

Most UI copy stays in the catalog. Served copy is for operational content that can change between
releases.

## Current served documents

- FAQ (`faq`)
- Make Clip how-to (`clip-how-to`)

## Versioned acceptance documents

Terms of Service and popularity tracking are not managed-copy slugs. Each one is versioned, carries
an agreement date, and is accepted or declined by the account:

- `GET /legal/terms` (public) — short intro plus full markdown for the configured terms version
- `GET /legal/popularity-tracking` (authenticated) — same shape for the popularity-tracking version

Do not add a `terms` or `popularity-tracking` managed-copy slug, and do not fold either document
into `GET /managed-copy/:slug`.

## Rules

- Do not add bundled fallback prose for served documents in app code or locale JSON.
- Always render loading and retry states while fetching served documents.
- Add new managed-copy docs by adding locale markdown files plus allowlisted slug support, not by
  creating a new endpoint for each document. Versioned acceptance documents are the exception
  above: they stay on `/legal/*`.

Reference: [754-server-managed-copy-endpoint](/docs/proposals/mobile/_master-plan_/phase-2/details/754-server-managed-copy-endpoint.md)
